# Everything the build does not need. Without this the whole node_modules tree
# and every build artefact is sent to the daemon as context, which is slow and
# can silently overwrite the image's own install.
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
e2e/test-results
e2e/playwright-report
docs
*.md
!README.md

# `**/` is load-bearing: a bare `.env.local` matches only a root-level file,
# and the one that matters is at `apps/web/.env.local`. Without the glob it
# rides into the image through `COPY . .`, and a dev's mocks-on flag gets
# baked into a production bundle — which the app then announces at startup,
# but only to whoever is reading that console.
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
